RESOLUTION OF THE FIRST BOARD OF DIRECTORS OF [COMPANY NAME] LIMITED (the 'Company') PASSED ON [DATE] AT [TIME] AT [REGISTERED OFFICE ADDRESS]

WHEREAS the Company was incorporated under the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) of Hong Kong on [DATE] with Certificate of Incorporation No. [NUMBER];

WHEREAS the Articles of Association of the Company authorize the Board of Directors to exercise all powers of the Company, including the power to issue shares, open bank accounts, adopt a registered office, and appoint officers;

WHEREAS the initial subscribers have subscribed for [NUMBER] ordinary shares of HKD [VALUE] each, and the Board deems it necessary to formally record the allotment of such shares;

WHEREAS the Company intends to commence business operations and requires banking facilities, a registered office, and statutory officers to comply with legal obligations;

NOW THEREFORE, IT IS HEREBY RESOLVED AS FOLLOWS:

1. SHARE CAPITAL SUBSCRIPTION: That the allotment and issuance of [NUMBER] ordinary shares of HKD [VALUE] each, fully paid, to the initial subscribers as set forth in the register of members, be and is hereby ratified, confirmed, and approved. The Board authorizes the Company Secretary to file the necessary return of allotment with the Companies Registry within one month.

2. BANKING AUTHORIZATION: That the Company shall open and maintain bank accounts with [BANK NAME] and any other financial institutions as the Board may determine. The Board hereby authorizes [NAME OF DIRECTOR] and [NAME OF DIRECTOR] (jointly or severally) to sign all banking documents, cheques, and instructions on behalf of the Company, subject to any limits set by the Board.

3. REGISTERED OFFICE ADOPTION: That the registered office of the Company shall be situated at [FULL ADDRESS IN HONG KONG], and the Company Secretary is directed to file the necessary notice of change of registered office with the Companies Registry if required.

4. STATUTORY OFFICER APPOINTMENTS: That [NAME] be and is hereby appointed as the first Director of the Company, and [NAME] be and is hereby appointed as the Company Secretary, each to hold office until the next annual general meeting or until their successors are duly appointed. The Board authorizes the Company Secretary to file all statutory declarations and returns as required by the Companies Ordinance.

5. GENERAL AUTHORIZATION: That any director or the company secretary be and is hereby authorized to execute all documents, make all filings, and take all actions necessary to give effect to the foregoing resolutions.

This resolution is effective immediately and shall be recorded in the minutes of the first board meeting.
